        "title": "Volume 6 Diamond - History and Ideas II",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "Agriculture did not emerge from trial and error alone. It emerged from fertility ritual — the observation that seed placed in earth returns multiplied, wrapped in a narrative of death and resurrection (Osiris, Persephone, the corn god). The ritual calendar preceded the planting calendar. The myth structured the practice before the practice yielded data."
    },
